     "page": 1,
     "text": "[FAX] p.1 ---- Kennedy Group Clinic\n\npt Patterson dob 04/21/51\n\n03/27 - kidney stones bp 145/91 wt 187 f/u 3mo\n\nPatient Timothy Patterson 75 years presented for follow-up on his kidney stones. BP 145/91, weight 187 lbs. Pt reports occasional flank pain but no acute episodes in past 3 months. Non-compliant with tamsulosin, reports forgetting to take regularly. Instructed on importance of medication adherence. Follow-up in 3 months.\n\n07/23 - lab review bp 144/83 wt 189 f/u 3mo\n\nMr. Patterson came in routine lab review. BP 144/83, weight 189 lbs. results within normal limits. Pt reports no new complaints. Follow-up in 3 months.\n\n11/18 - urinary tract infection bp 154/90 wt 784 ok\n\nPt presented with dysuria and frequency. UTI via urinalysis. BP 154/90, weight 184 lbs. Prescribed sulfamethoxazole-trimethoprim and nitrofurantoin. Pt resolution of symptoms after 1 week of antibiotics. No further complaints.\n\n03/15 - urinary tract infection bp 151/81 wt 196 f/u Patterson returned with recurrent UTI. BP 151/81, weight 196 lbs. Treated with another course of sulfamethoxazole-trimethoprim and nitrofurantoin. Pt reports improvement after 1 week. Follow-up in 3 months.\n\n07/12 - kidney stones bp 145/86 wt 199 ok\n\nPt presented acute flank pain, diagnosed as kidney BP 145/86, weight 199 lbs. Pain resolved with conservative management. Instructed on tamsulosin for stone passage. No further - kidney stones bp 141/91 198 cont meds\n\nFollow-up visit for kidney stones. BP 141/91, weight 198 lbs. Pt reports no new stone episodes. Instructed to continue tamsulosin. Non-compliant with follow-up appointments x2.\n\n03/04 - bp 147/82 wt 188 f/u 3mo\n\nPt presented with pruritic rash on arms. BP 147/82, weight 188 Likely allergic treated with topical steroids. Rash resolved after 1 Follow-up in 3 months.\n\nDx: urinary tract infection; kidney stones; gout\n\nNote: patient with medications; missed appointments alcohol ~4 drinks/week\n\nPt has history of recurrent urinary tract infections, managed with sulfamethoxazole-trimethoprim nitrofurantoin. Kidney stones managed with tamsulosin, though pt non-compliant. Gout controlled on colchicine and allopurinol. Pt drinks approximately 4 alcoholic per week. Family history significant for father with COPD at age 79.\n\nPt has been non-compliant with medications and missed 2 follow-up appointments. Importance of adherence discussed at each visit. No acute complaints at last visit on 03/27/2026."
